One library, several ways to hold it. Same CapTP conversation on the wire;
choose the surface that matches how you work.

[One core under all three surfaces, so the one you hold never changes what a session puts on the wire.]($image.siteAsset('diagram-surfaces.svg'))

| Surface | You write | Reach for it when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Zig package]($link.page('start')) | Zig | you want the full engine and types |
| [C ABI](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/consuming-from-c.md) | C / any FFI | embedding, or wrapping a language with no binding yet |
| [Bindings]($link.page('bindings')) | Rust, TypeScript, Python, Racket | you are already in one of those four |
| [CapTP CLI]($link.page('cli')) | shell / MCP | call, host, REPL, or agent MCP (`zig build pancake`) |

## Zig

`zig fetch --save git+https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake`, import `pancake`,
use owning `Session`. Line-by-line first round-trip: [Start]($link.page('start')).
Chapters: [examples](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/examples/README.md).
Declarations: [Zig API]($link.page('reference/api')).

## C ABI

Composable archives (`.a` and the platform shared library), each with a
generated header. Opaque handles, fixed-width codes, `ptr + len`, callbacks,
explicit release. Inventory: [API reference]($link.page('reference')). First
program: [consuming-from-c](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/consuming-from-c.md).

## Bindings

Each binding wraps the same archives in that language's idioms. Shared shape and
binding-check steps: [Bindings]($link.page('bindings')).

## CapTP CLI

The product binary lives under repo-root `cli/`: progressive `ocapn` commands, a
REPL, curated stdio MCP, and `app rooms-peer`. It is not a second protocol
stack. Happy path: [CapTP CLI]($link.page('cli')). Recipes:
[docs/cli.md](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/cli.md).

## One engine

A Zig peer, a C consumer, and any binding hold the same OCapN conversation byte
for byte. Codec and CapTP version settle with whoever answers, not with which
surface you built on. See [Concepts]($link.page('concepts')). Every artifact
comes from `zig build`; `zig build check` is the in-tree verification. Common
steps:
[README](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/README.md#build).
Encryption is optional iroh: [Transports]($link.page('transports')).
